<title>LEBANON: Lebanon trade deficit widens in May.</title>
<headline>Lebanon trade deficit widens in May.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's trade deficit for the first five months of 1997 rose to $2,673 million from $2,518 million in the same period of 1996, according to customs figures released on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The May deficit rose to $600 million from $592 million in April and from $519 million in May 1996.</p>
<p>The High Customs Council issued the following figures (in millions of U.S. dollars):</p>
<p>	  MERCHANDISE TRADE</p>
<p>					 May97    Apr97    Mar97	May</p>
<p>96</p>
<p>	  Monthly</p>
<p>	  Exports		   49	 47	 69	   83</p>
<p>	  Imports		  649	639	615	  602</p>
<p>	  Trade balance</p>
<p>	  year-to-date</p>
<p>	  Exports		  317	268	220	  375</p>
<p>	  Imports		2,990    2,341    1,702	2,893</p>
<p>	  Balance	     -2,673   -2,073   -1,482     -2,518</p>
<p>	  - Beirut editorial (9611) 645307  745308  602057</p>
</text>
